// A value whose type nothing ever says is a value the chapters refuse:
// `Option::None` needs the option it *is*, and nothing here names one —
// the `let` has no annotation and the family is what asked, the same
// refusal Ch. 4 §2.3 writes down for the binding that left `T` without
// a word of its own. Both implementations refuse it by name, and what
// each says of why is the one thing they are not held to (G9.181's
// own, beside the ones that went the other way).

fn main() -> t27 {
    let a = Option::None;
    0
}
